# Redirects for this Worker's static assets.
#
# Deliberately empty of rules.
#
# This project deploys as a Worker with static assets (`wrangler deploy`), which
# serves exactly one hostname per deployment and only accepts relative paths
# here. An earlier version of this file tried to do apex-to-www canonicalisation
# and failed the build: the source was an absolute URL and the status carried a
# Pages-style "301!" force suffix, neither of which this parser supports.
#
# It is moot now regardless. The canonical host is the bare apex
# (https://thepeacemakerbrewster.com) and that is exactly what this Worker
# serves, so there is no host-level hop to perform. If a www -> apex redirect is
# ever wanted, it belongs in a zone-level Redirect Rule, not here; see DEPLOY.md.
#
# If a same-host, path-only redirect is ever needed (e.g. an old URL that
# moved), the working syntax here is:
#   /old-path  /new-path  301
